  "interpretation": [
    "Consumer-only nonzero RMW loses roughly 9\u201335% throughput relative to atomics at the tested tuned shapes; producer cost reduces the observed chain regression.",
    "Known-zero consumer benefit reaches about 3% but producer-inclusive ratios are within about 0.5% of baseline at tuned shapes; this does not justify a native extension on performance grounds.",
    "Extra indirect memory traffic is a plausible explanation for RMW regression, not a profiled causal conclusion.",
    "This kernel already uses relaxed atomics. An ordering control is needed before attributing the previous embedding gains solely to atomic removal."
  ],
